For rk_remove_matching_lines: walk with memchr(line, '\n', remaining) to
find line boundaries. For each line, call rk_target_substring_match(). If
it returns false, memmove the line to write_pos and advance write_pos.
Return write_pos as the new length.

For rk_read_return: check result > 0 && result <= RK_BUF_MAX. Skip if
content_targets.count == 0. Copy user buffer into scratch with
copy_from_user_nofault. Call rk_remove_matching_lines on scratch. If
new_len != result, copy back with copy_to_user_nofault and set the
return value to new_len with regs_set_return_value.

For rk_tcp_show_pre: get v from regs->si. Check v != SEQ_START_TOKEN.
Cast v to struct sock*, get inet_sk(sk)->inet_sport. Convert with
ntohs() and check rk_target_number_match(&port_targets, port). Return
1 to hide, 0 to show.

For rk_write: strip trailing newline. Use strncmp to match "hide content ",
"hide port ", "unhide content ", "unhide port ". For hide, call
rk_target_add with the rest of the string. For unhide, parse the index
with kstrtouint and call rk_target_remove.

For init: init both lists, register_kretprobe(&read_probe),
register_kprobe(&tcp_probe), proc_create("rklings", 0600, ...).
Unwind on failure. Exit in reverse order.
